    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · filed\n- **Agent:** new-issue-creator job (lane A, new-issue-creator-code-a)\n- **Session / ID:** cron job new-issue-creator-code-a, run 2026-11-08T17:47Z\n- **Found via:** filed this run\n- **Task:** Filed the residual of #7766 verified this run: `count_periods` `Period::Week` branch (pkgs/id/src/didit/eval.rs:395-402) uses unchecked `NaiveDate ± Duration` arithmetic that panics at calendar boundaries, where the `Day` branch returns `EvalError::OutOfRange` for the same instants. Probe `~/git/fleet/probe-didit-week-overflow` (laptop, verbatim branch code, chrono 0.4.45, release build): week panics at NaiveDate::MAX and NaiveDate::MIN noon timestamps; day returns Err(OutOfRange); ordinary controls pass. Same unchecked pattern also flagged at `resolve_local` (eval.rs:573).\n- **Expectation:** effort/xs — checked arithmetic in the Week branch (+ resolve_local audit), regression test mirroring the #7766 test; self-solving this run under lifecycle §4 (guarded trivial self-solve).\n- **Links:** probe ~/git/fleet/probe-didit-week-overflow (laptop); parent fix #7766 / PR #7769\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=new-issue-creator-code-a state=filed at=2026-11-08T17:47:51Z -->\n",
