    "body": "🤖 **Agent note** · done\n- **Agent:** new-issue-creator job (lane A, new-issue-creator-code-a)\n- **Session / ID:** cron job new-issue-creator-code-a, run 2026-11-08T17:47Z\n- **Found via:** self-assigned during new-issue-creator-code-a run (guarded trivial self-solve, lifecycle protocol §4)\n- **Task:** Fixed: `Period::Week` branch of `count_periods` (pkgs/id/src/didit/eval.rs) now uses `checked_sub_signed`/`checked_add_signed` for the Monday offset, `monday + 7d`, and `monday - 7d`, mapping unrepresentable dates to `EvalError::OutOfRange`; `resolve_local`'s +1h DST-gap shift is checked the same way (falls through to the UTC interpretation); the #7766 comment no longer claims the Week branch is calendar-guarded. Regression test `week_period_at_calendar_boundary_is_out_of_range_not_a_panic` added.\n- **Expectation:** met — PR #7773 merged as 00ca41860980985d37347c7c67bd3c526382a455. Verification (laptop): probe pre-fix panics at NaiveDate::MAX/MIN (release, verbatim code); new test panics pre-fix at eval.rs:396 (mutation check via stash) and passes with the fix; `cargo test --lib didit::` 29/29 on the branch and 29/29 re-run on merged main at 00ca418609. PR CI was still runner-queued at merge; merged under the standing merge authority on the strength of the laptop verification. No queue packet (§4 self-solve).\n- **Links:** PR #7773 (merged 00ca418609); branch creator-a/7771-didit-week-overflow @625be71066; probe ~/git/fleet/probe-didit-week-overflow\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=new-issue-creator-code-a state=done at=2026-11-08T17:59:00Z -->\n",
